  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;Right Side&quot; Human Rights Defender Non Governmental Organization</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Right Side is a community-based, community-led, democratic, human rights defender NGO, founded in 2016 by trans activists in Armenia. Aiming to challenge and transform power for trans, lesbian, bisexual, queer, non-binary women, sex workers and other marginalized women, Right Side employs several strategies: raising of visibility of trans, queer and non-binary women, advocacy to influence laws and policies, service provision with mental health and legal support.   The grant will support the following specific priorities and activities: - Organizational Strengthening - Educating and equipping marginalized women with the tools and capacities to hold people in positions of power to account, demand for their rights and take actions to restore their fundamental freedoms - Advocacy for advancement of legal gaps, effectively addressing anti-discrimination, hate speech/crimes and legal gender recognition - Legal Research - Movement Building</narrative>
  </description>
